    "pyqtgraph_version": "0.14.0",
    "pyqtgraph_commit": "a20028b98294b9cc8770f2015a92eb342224b788",
    "source": "pyqtgraph/functions.py makeQImage",
    "notes": [
      "Rank-3 channel order follows PyQtGraph's documented (b, g, r, a) order.",
      "Rank-3 three-channel input defaults to RGB32 with opaque alpha; forcing alpha=true selects ARGB32 with opaque alpha.",
      "Rank-3 four-channel input defaults to ARGB32 and preserves alpha; alpha=false selects RGB32 and discards input alpha.",
      "Rank-2 grayscale input is supported with the documented transpose semantics, while the pinned Python implementation raises for transpose=true because it calls transpose((1, 0, 2)) on a 2D array.",
      "The C++ helper returns an owned copied QImage. The copy option is accepted for API parity and does not change ownership behavior."
    ]
  },
